# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Repository hygiene for the ML price-modelling project.
#
#  Everything listed here is REGENERATED output or local state — none of it
#  belongs in version control. Measured on 20 October 2026, the untracked tree
#  held 50,206 files / 3.5 GB, which made `git status` take minutes and left a
#  single `git add .` able to break the repository (GitHub rejects files over
#  100 MB, and several model.pkl / candle-index files are well past that).
#
#  Rule of thumb: if a script can recreate it, it does not get committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Generated simulation output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# price_modeling.py writes data_N.csv / image_N.png pairs here (410 MB, 50k files)
stock_testing/generator/looped_results/
# market_analysis.py and ml_model.py artefacts, incl. GB-scale candle indexes (3.1 GB)
stock_testing/generator/looped_analysis/
# analyze_looped_results.R output
stock_testing/generator/looped_results_analysis_300/
# archives written when [storage] archive_after_run = true in config.toml
stock_testing/generator/looped_results_*.zip
**/archived_runs.zip

# ── Trained models and large binary artefacts ────────────────────────────────
# A single forest from a 50k-run batch is ~4.4 MB; they are rebuilt by training.
*.pkl
*.joblib
# Columnar bulk storage. Phase 1 of the build manual moves the panel off CSV
# onto Parquet (idea 212); those files are large, generated, and rebuildable.
*.parquet
*.feather

# ── Generated reports (rebuild: python routine/daily_routine.py) ─────────────
stock_testing/generator/routine/reports/
stock_testing/generator/looped_analysis/summary_report.html
# NOTE: routine/routine_log.csv is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the
# accumulating day-by-day record and is worth keeping in history.

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── R ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# ── Secrets — never commit these ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Local backups ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Learn_backup.zip

# ── OS and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local run state - regenerated on every run, never worth committing
stock_testing/generator/routine/routine_state.json
# Run cards written beside the code by regime_check.py (idea 466): git commit,
# config hash, seed and volatility regime for one training run. Per-machine
# state, rewritten each run; the durable record belongs in the results ledger.
run_card_*.json

# ── HF dataset export staging and training output ────────────────────────────
# export_hf_dataset.py writes the Parquet splits, schema and data card here
# before pushing them to the private HF repo; all of it is regenerated by
# rerunning the exporter, and the pushed copy on the Hub is the real record.
stock_testing/generator/hf_staging/
# train_weighted.py output: model.pkl is already covered by *.pkl above, but
# metrics.json and training.log are rebuilt by every run and the numbers that
# matter are written into HF_EXPORT_AND_JOBS_REPORT.md.
stock_testing/generator/model_out/
